     $ =====================================================================         
     $ RBE3 TEST SERIES -- DECK 06: NEAR-ZERO-WEIGHT INDEPENDENT GRID                
     $ (EDGE CASE)                                                                   
     $                                                                               
     $ REFC=123 ONLY. THREE INDEPENDENT GRIDS: 751 (W=1.0), 752 (W=1.E-6),           
     $ 753 (W=2.0). GRID 752 IS GIVEN AN ARBITRARY, DELIBERATELY EXTREME             
     $ DISPLACEMENT (99., 99., 99.).                                                 
     $                                                                               
     $ [CORRECTION: THIS DECK ORIGINALLY USED W=0.0 EXACTLY FOR GRID 752.            
     $ MSC NASTRAN REJECTED THAT WITH *** USER FATAL MESSAGE 2038 (RBE3S):           
     $ RBE3 ELEMENT 40 IS SINGULAR -- CONFIRMED (BY RANK-CHECKING THE FULL           
     $ 6X6 RIGID-BODY-FIT SYSTEM) THIS IS BECAUSE A LITERAL ZERO WEIGHT              
     $ DROPS GRID 752 ENTIRELY, LEAVING ONLY 2 REMAINING POINTS (751, 753,           
     $ BOTH AT Z=0), ONE SHORT OF THE 3 NON-COLLINEAR POINTS NEEDED TO               
     $ DETERMINE ALL 6 RIGID-BODY MODES. FIXED WITH W=1.E-6.]                        
     $                                                                               
     $ [SECOND CORRECTION, MORE IMPORTANT: THIS DECK'S ORIGINAL "EXPECTED"           
     $ VALUE ASSUMED A NEAR-ZERO WEIGHT CONTRIBUTES NEGLIGIBLY TO A PLAIN            
     $ DECOUPLED WEIGHTED AVERAGE -- (99*1.E-6)/3 |= 3.3E-5. THAT                    
     $ ASSUMPTION IS WRONG. BUG #6 (SEE THE RBE3 SERIES README) ESTABLISHED          
     $ THAT A CORRECT RBE3 ALWAYS SOLVES THE FULL COUPLED 6-DOF RIGID-BODY           
     $ SYSTEM INTERNALLY, EVEN WHEN REFC=123 ONLY OUTPUTS THE TRANSLATION            
     $ PART. WITH THIS DECK'S SPECIFIC GEOMETRY (ALL 3 INDEPENDENT GRIDS             
     $ COPLANAR AT Z=0, GIVING WEAK/UNDERDETERMINED ROTATIONAL LEVERAGE),            
     $ GRID 752'S TINY WEIGHT ON AN EXTREME (99,99,99) VALUE IS NOT                  
     $ NEGLIGIBLE IN THE COUPLED SYSTEM -- IT MEANINGFULLY PERTURBS THE              
     $ RESULT THROUGH THE IMPLICIT ROTATIONAL COUPLING, EVEN THOUGH                  
     $ ROTATION ISN'T PART OF REFC OR THE OUTPUT. CONFIRMED BY TWO                   
     $ INDEPENDENT SOLVERS (PATCHED MYSTRAN AND COMLAB) AGREEING EXACTLY             
     $ ON THE CORRECTED VALUE BELOW, WHICH IS NOT THE NAIVE WEIGHTED                 
     $ AVERAGE.]                                                                     
     $                                                                               
     $ PURPOSE (REVISED): DEMONSTRATE THAT "NEAR-ZERO WEIGHT" IS NOT                 
     $ SIMPLY NEGLIGIBLE IN ISOLATION -- WHETHER IT MATTERS DEPENDS ON THE           
     $ FULL COUPLED SYSTEM, NOT JUST THE DIRECTLY-OUTPUT COMPONENT'S OWN             
     $ DECOUPLED ARITHMETIC. THIS DECK NO LONGER DEMONSTRATES "NEGLIGIBLE            
     $ WEIGHT IS NEGLIGIBLE"; IT DEMONSTRATES THE OPPOSITE, AND IS A GOOD            
     $ REGRESSION CHECK THAT THE BUG #6 FIX'S COUPLING IS GENUINELY ACTIVE           
     $ FOR A CASE WHERE IT HAS A LARGE, VISIBLE EFFECT.                              
     $                                                                               
     $ EXPECTED RESULT, GRID 750 (CONFIRMED BY MYSTRAN POST-FIX AND COMLAB,          
     $ EXACT AGREEMENT TO 6 SIGNIFICANT FIGURES):                                    
     $   T1 = 0.335339   T2 = -0.035273   T3 = 19.760000                             
     $ NOT THE NAIVE DECOUPLED WEIGHTED AVERAGE (0.300033, 0.000033,                 
     $ -0.083300) THAT AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS FILE INCORRECTLY                   
     $ DOCUMENTED AS "EXPECTED."                                                     
